comments.body:
@brianquinlan, it works using [package:cronet_http](https://pub.dev/packages/cronet_http) on Android Devices!

However please be aware that this HTTP client won't support the classic "badCertificateCallback" to manage self signed certificates  without creating a custom CA to install on all the machines you want to use (https://github.com/dart-lang/http/issues/1314) ^^

It should be doable by using the native `CronetEngine.Builder(..)` with a drugged ` TrustManager`  that will accept any certificate by your own specific internal logic, but as far as I understood, the current flutter package `cronet_http `  doesn't allow to add this options on the native `CronetEngine`

